{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates architectural ambition but suffers from critical D96A EANCOM INVOIC incompleteness and semantic flattening. The model defines only 9 of ~18 mandatory segment types, lacks qualifier-based distinctions (treating all NAD/DTM/MOA as homogeneous), and conflates syntactic structure with business semantics through improper class hierarchies. The 'business layer' (Invoice, LineItem) exists in isolation from EDIFACT segments, violating the standard's compositional logic.",
  "completeness_score": 0.35,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "PAISegment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Payment Instructions (PAI) is mandatory in D96A EANCOM INVOIC for specifying payment terms. Missing entirely."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "ALCSegment_Charges",
      "priority": "high",
